# @podlite/mcp

=head1 Upcoming

=item C<podlite_query> reports a source or an address in the selector that does not resolve as an error of the tool; it returned no matches

=item the query tool selects from the tree C<convert> reads, so a Markdown section is read into blocks, and gives a found block as C<podlite query> does. It is given text, not a file, so an C<=include> in it is not resolved

=head1 0.0.18

=item the package declares an exports map and its own type entry, and no longer points at an esm build it never produced. A bundler that preferred that entry resolved to a missing file

=head1 0.0.3

=item declare public npm access so the package publishes to the registry

=head1 0.0.2

=item initial release: MCP stdio server with four tools — C<podlite_parse> (source to AST with locations), C<podlite_validate> (parse errors + lint rules + schema check), C<podlite_render> (HTML/Markdown), C<podlite_query> (structural selector over blocks)
